{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-space-tuple","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0076","math_ordinal":190,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH21-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Part 213D(d) has just proved local determination for the c.l.d. version.  The concluding tuple must therefore be the tilde space, not the original measure space.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt213.tex:257","source_normalized_sha256":"05e9b769403b4c7926a944d5aaa03f00bb216412bc3f850e41b3c28de657aa67","source_text":"$(X,\\Sigma,\\mu)$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt213.tex:260","target_normalized_sha256":"3e134a815dc912ab5b295db4411e9f08536230e6a0834f40378e0190aec12436","target_text":"$(X,\\tilde\\Sigma,\\tilde\\mu)$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S213"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-bound-variable","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0077","math_ordinal":229,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH21-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The supremum ranges over measurable subsets F of H.  E is otherwise free in this set-builder, while the following proof consistently chooses and varies F.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt213.tex:298","source_normalized_sha256":"79eef544bd0a0b95ad2c91a0bdf39faeb5a53ff98633eb7a2736a59d5dee5c29","source_text":"$\\tilde\\mu H=\\sup\\{\\mu F:E\\in\\Sigma$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt213.tex:301","target_normalized_sha256":"3c939ad24373944bef1be5a9c63af8dd571afac3a55755438099adbed172f7a7","target_text":"$\\tilde\\mu H=\\sup\\{\\mu F:F\\in\\Sigma$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S213"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-measure-component","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0078","math_ordinal":466,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH21-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Here H is only assumed to belong to tilde-Sigma, so H symmetric-difference F need not lie in the domain of mu.  It does lie in the domain of tilde-mu, which is the measure used throughout 213H.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt213.tex:575","source_normalized_sha256":"77a233e0e0ddab89db7bf686afd46faf16dd7a6d5087ed3ece3382eaf56d2f2e","source_text":"$\\mu(H\\symmdiff F)=0$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt213.tex:588","target_normalized_sha256":"3b3571b51b29cc841f8e24ade83cdff127de7e7370d09707ed263a89918a3b86","target_text":"$\\tilde\\mu(H\\symmdiff F)=0$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S213"}
{"classification":"mathematical-circular-piecewise-condition","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0079","math_ordinal":687,"provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH21-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"The display is defining h from the extended-real-valued function h*.  Its first branch must test whether h*(x) is real; testing h(x) is circular because h has not yet been defined.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt213.tex:823","source_normalized_sha256":"48d2c7f1fbd4f6d52115d8f78cb3dcebc955b57a51f7222b8675f3ea610e19d2","source_text":"$h(x)\\in\\Bbb R$","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt213.tex:840","target_normalized_sha256":"2c80d09236324accc65ac988e4bcb60df941508adc1a6a9616ca75f78fe33977","target_text":"$h^*(x)\\in\\Bbb R$","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S213"}
{"classification":"mathematical-wrong-property-name","correction_applied":true,"id":"O007-CORR-0080","provenance":{"basis":"exact current source-correction ledger row","kind":"source-correction-ledger","source_resource_ids":["O007-RESOURCE-CH21-SOURCE-CORRECTIONS"]},"rationale":"Exercise 213Xh points back to 213I, whose defined property is locally determined negligible sets.  The measurable-set wording names a different property and does not state the intended implication to semi-finiteness.","record_type":"source_correction","rights_id":"O007-RIGHTS-FREMLIN-DSL","schema_version":"1.1.0","source_locator":"authority/fremlin/source/mt2.2016/mt213.tex:1068-1069","source_text":"locally determined measurable sets","target_locator":"source/id-ID/mt213.tex:1087-1088","target_text":"himpunan terabaikan yang ditentukan secara lokal","unit_id":"O007-FREMLIN-V2-S213"}
